# Coordinates for the native degree-120 comparison

These constants transcribe `source/adjoint120-comparison.json`. Rows are packed
in binary and matrices act on columns. No identity is asserted by this file;
the native interpretation and comparison identities are separate proofs.
The eleven code coordinates use Golay rows 0 through 10 modulo constants.
The adjoint coordinates are off-diagonal matrix units in lexicographic order,
then E_ii + E_10,10 for i < 10.

Sources: James, J. Algebra 27 (1973), 57–111; GM02, Proposition 5.1.
-/

